From eee92f3087f6be51005fd172a65a7b43ee7781ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] perf(kanban-sync): divergence repair compares
 settled cards in SQLite; chat-link pass off the round thread

Hub 2026-11-13 after #1843 (t_01a1d2cc49634a78): replica pulled_at 04:14:01 -> 04:26:48 (13 min stale), the
remote-parent mirror held finished worker cards as running, so hub children did not promote.

- py-spy record 04:17Z (gw 1817115, sync thread 1819025, 1626 samples incl. idle): 100% in
  repair_divergence; 84% at the `SELECT * FROM tasks` fetchall over every live card (5,496 rows), 15% at the
  replica chunk reads. Each fetched row re-acquires the contended gateway GIL: a SELECT * fetch of 1000 rows
  takes 0.01 s alone and 4-10 s with 1-3 CPU-bound threads in the process (repro on worker-4, Python 3.14).
  Fix: `_differing_settled` joins live and replica in one read-only SQLite connection (replica ATTACHed
  read-only) and returns only the ids whose synced columns differ (run refs compared by uid). Equal raw values
  give equal `_row_fields`, so it is a superset; each candidate is re-compared exactly as before. Unattachable
  files fall back to the full scan. 60 settled cards + 1 edit: 121 `_row_fields` conversions at base, 2 at head.
- The chat-link pass ran inline in the loop: 04:14-04:24Z one pass (its strict ledger read queued on
  `_links_lock`) held the round ~10 min. It now runs on its own `kanban-sync-links` thread with its own
  connection scope; the loop requests a pass on its cadence and a request while one runs is refused (no pile-up).
  Test: with a pass blocked, all 6 rounds run before it returns (base: 1 of 6).
